{
  "description": "The spec types every PATCH body as io.k8s.apimachinery.pkg.apis.meta.v1.Patch, a bare object, which convert drops, and names the patch types only in `consumes`. Patch operations had no body member, and a patch passed as extra keys went out as application/json, which the API server refuses with 415 Unsupported Media Type (kube-apiserver v1.36.2, 2026-10-29). Each patch operation gets a required `body` document and a required `contentType` header that names the patch type, as client-go does. application/apply-patch+cbor is left out: it needs a body of CBOR bytes.",
